# Local WSL Auto-Validation

After every turn that edits `lib/**`, `test/**`, `web/**`, `docker/**`, `pubspec.yaml`, or `assets/data/**`, **run validation in WSL** before marking work complete. **Do not** write augmentation-log entries until the full plan run finishes (`ai-augmentation.mdc`).

## Command matrix

| Trigger | WSL commands |
|---------|----------------|
| Any code/data change | `flutter pub get && flutter analyze && flutter test` |
| UI, routing, or feature slice | + `bash scripts/wsl_dev.sh` (background); smoke `http://localhost:3000/` |
| docker/nginx/pubspec/deploy | Tier 2: `bash scripts/wsl_deploy.sh`; verify `/` and `/session/s-001` refresh |
| End of plan run / before push | Tier 1 green **and** Tier 2 green **and** coverage gate green |

Windows host prefix: `wsl -e bash -lc 'cd /mnt/c/Nagarro/ai-avengers && <cmd>'`

## Plan compliance (accumulate, log once at end)

Compare completed scope against the active plan in `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md` (prefer v5 uplift or current v6 slice). Track (do not log yet):
- Plan todos still pending after the run
- Violations of `flo-compass-product.mdc`, web-only, mock-first, or deep-link guardrails
- Missing tests, a11y, or docs the plan requires

## On pass or fail

1. **Fix blockers** in the same turn when feasible (analyze errors, failing tests, 404 deep links).
2. **Hold results** for the single batched augmentation entry: Tier 1/2 status, smoke notes, plan gaps, corrections.
3. **Do not report plan/run as complete** to the user until the augmentation-log entry is written (implementation) or drafted (plan-only). Write the entry only after all agents stop and the requested plan scope is complete (`ai-augmentation.mdc`).

## Skip validation only when

- Read-only Q&A with zero file edits
- Pure `hackathon-docs/` prose with no code/data impact

## Do not

- Claim a plan run is done without final Tier 1 at minimum
- Claim a plan run is done without an augmentation-log entry (`ai-augmentation.mdc`)
- Skip Tier 2 after docker/nginx/routing changes or before push
- Log augmentation entries per phase or per validation step
- Run `flutter`/`docker` from PowerShell as the primary workflow
- Change ARM/CI for local convenience (`wsl2-development.mdc`)

